              `NOT_SENT_WHY` in forged.test.ts `WRITTEN` encodes the same overreach:
              - an Unsent `Rejected` on a lane, which cells.ts:252-308 never gives;
              - a Declined `Cancelled` or `StorageRefused`;
              - an Answered success whose reason is not `success`.

              Replayed: an Unsent Rejected is heard as `AddNotSent`. Each one gives only an ending that a swap to
              another valid reason (Q4) can already give.
            - Actor writer against the strict decode (owner @task.V3.T92). `recordFour` admits shapes `encodeActor`
              never writes:
              - a reactions count other than the machine's;
              - empty, equal or unreferenced memory copies, and copy fields the machine never declared;
              - schedules of states outside the current chain;
              - graph bindings to any declared machine, under any slot name.

              No test encodes a decoded record and compares the result, though Codec I7 claims round-trip. Nothing
              replayed wrong: no fixture has an owing consumer whose provider has slots.
            - Q4 (the user's read). Confirmed that a per-record decode cannot tell an `Answered` success beside a Held
              head of the same Attempt: the lane record and the owed record are separate (@spec.WriteAhead.R5).
              Replayed: `Added`, then the next Add gets `AddNotSent` (stuck key), and a retry would re-invoke a write
              already heard as succeeded. `decodeRecords` sees the whole store, so a boot-wide "one Attempt, ended once"
              check is possible. The same holds for a displaced Attempt whose ending is also owed.
            - The deep format-1 record matches Restore R5: the slot Schema refuses the form, so the slot is unselected.
              No ending is lost: `seen` and baselines drive only reactions, and an unselected slot can only add a fire,
              as with any refused format-1 form. Its test asserts only `lifecycle` (low).
            - The input-field patch matches Compile R7 and Turn R13 (a refused turn is InvalidTurn), and no fixture
              patches an input field. In production, where memory is unfrozen, an update that mutates an input field in
              place passes the check (@task.V3.T98, low). Compile.spec:70-71 have trailing spaces.
            - Low (owner @task.V3.T92):
              - the walker caches in `record.ts` are hand WeakMaps with no measurement;
              - records.test.ts uses temporary "held for the user" strings;
              - the new comments in core are not doc comments.

            Sidecars (each finding re-checked):

            - Accepted after replay:
              - blind: the ending followed by another row (blocking 1);
              - blind and census: an Unsent Rejected on a lane (routed);
              - blind: Q4 cross-record (routed).
            - Accepted by reading:
